    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d639">

                <pb facs="0750" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2895: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bell</hi>)<anchor n="9" xml:id="d639-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-27T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>286. Department’s November 29, 1 p.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d639-f2"/> Under date
                    of July 20th the American Group and the Pacific Development Corporation informed
                    the Department that arrangements had finally been completed for the taking over
                    by the former of the Corporation’s option under the loan contract entered into
                    between the Corporation and the Chinese Government on November 26, 1919.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d639-f3"/></p>
                <p>On July 24th, the Department informed the Group and the Corporation that in view
                    of the arrangements agreed upon between them, the Department is now prepared to
                    recognize and support the loan contract of November 26, 1919. It will be
                    observed, therefore, that the Pacific Development Corporation loan is now merged
                    into the Consortium. On the same date a telegram<anchor n="8" xml:id="d639-f4"/>
                    was sent to the American Legation at Peking asking to be informed whether the
                    Chinese Government has granted an extension of the option under the contract or
                    whether it has been agreed that it shall run for a period of seven months after
                    the American Associate Inspector of the Wine and Tobacco Administration enters
                    upon his duties.</p>
                <p>You will communicate the substance of the above to the Japanese Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
